  "notes": "The percussion is the beat. Six lanes — shaker, conga, bongo, rim, clave, woodblock — each sprinkle 4–9 hits a bar across the 16ths, which is around ten times what the snare plays and is the whole claim of this model: it is percussion-led, not backbeat-led. The 3-2 lean is carried by the hat stream, whose likeliest base is `tresillo` grouped 3-3-3-3-4, so the accents land on 16th-steps 1, 4, 7, 10 and 13. The kick anchors 1, the a-of-2 and the 4 and then fills to 3–5 with a heavy offbeat lean. ⚠ The backbeat is one quiet snare on 2 and 4, dragged 4–9 ms late, with ghosts at 1a and 3& at 18–34% velocity — the side-stick colour comes from the `rim` perc lane, because `percs` is a density and the snare lane is the only thing that can play a backbeat. Harmony is bright and split roughly evenly between major and minor, a seventh on most chords, four-chord loops; the bass is its own singable riff rather than a doubling of the kick, which is why this kit has no 808 lane at all.",
